{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01GekKKF1uexuJndjtSnZS3z","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"```yaml\ntier: median\nnarrative_guidance: >\n  C1/C2 在 2 judges 范围内成立，claims 加 scope qualifier \"across the two judges tested\"。\n  C3 GEE gradient 定位为 empirical finding 非 generalizable insight。\n  Register 降为 method boundary case study。Blindspot 定位为 \"measurement sensitivity gap \n  documented in controlled setting\"。第 3 judge 仅覆盖 formality 1 axis，提供方向确认但不够升级 scope。\n  Findings 3.0–3.5 稳定落位。\n\nimagined_experiments:\n  - name: \"Multi-judge formality pairwise (partial — 1/2 judges completed)\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-001\"\n    description: >\n      Claude-3.5-Sonnet 完成 formality pairwise+Likert scoring（100 pairs × 2 directions）。\n      Gemini-2.0-Flash 因 API 额度耗尽仅完成 ~40% calls，数据不足以纳入正式分析。\n      最终仅新增 1 个 judge 的 formality 完整数据。\n    expected_results:\n      claude_bt_win_prob: 0.62\n      claude_bt_ci: [0.54, 0.70]\n      claude_bt_p: 0.005\n      claude_likert_ate: 0.03\n      claude_likert_p: 0.42\n      claude_likert_tie_rate: 0.68\n      claude_likert_cohens_d: 0.03\n      claude_consistency_rate: 0.58\n      claude_blindspot_confirmed: true\n      claude_gee_formal_or: 2.80\n      claude_gee_formal_p: 0.006\n      claude_gee_originality_or: 2.10\n      claude_gee_originality_p: 0.03\n      gemini_status: \"incomplete (~80/200 pairwise calls, excluded from analysis)\"\n      gemini_partial_formal_win_trend: \"~64% on available data, consistent direction\"\n      total_api_spend: \"$32 (Claude $22 + Gemini partial $10)\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Claude-3.5-Sonnet 作为 Anthropic proprietary model，style sensitivity 预期介于 GPT-4o (63.0%)\n      和 Qwen3-32B (66.5%) 之间偏低端。原因：(1) Claude 系列以 \"helpful, harmless\" 训练，对 style \n      的 systematic preference 可能弱于 Qwen 的 RLHF-heavy 训练，(2) BT 0.62 处于 tier 定义的\n      [0.58, 0.78] 区间下端，反映 \"方向确认但非最强信号\"。\n      Likert ATE NS (p=0.42) 延续 Blindspot pattern：tie rate ~68% 与其他 judge 一致（GPT-4o 62.5%,\n      Qwen 72.7%），表明 Likert insensitivity 是 measurement structure 问题而非 judge-specific。\n      GEE decomposition 显示 formality-originality mixed pattern（与 GPT-4o/Qwen 同方向），\n      OR 值略高于 GPT-4o (2.21) 但低于 Qwen (4.20)——不同 judge 内部权重分配不同但 pattern 一致。\n      Gemini 不完整是典型 median 档资源约束：~$30/judge × 2 judges 超出实际可用 API 预算弹性，\n      第二个 judge 被 cut。论文只能脚注提及 \"partial directional evidence from a third judge\"。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Cross-judge formality BT summary\"\n        content: |\n          | Judge        | BT P(formal) | 95% CI        | p       | Likert ATE | Likert p | Blindspot |\n          |-------------|-------------|---------------|---------|------------|----------|-----------|\n          | GPT-4o       | 0.630       | [0.558, 0.703] | <0.001  | ~0.08      | 0.332    | ✅        |\n          | Qwen3-32B    | 0.665       | [0.585, 0.739] | <0.0001 | 0.011      | 0.908    | ✅        |\n          | Claude-3.5   | 0.620       | [0.540, 0.700] | 0.005   | 0.03       | 0.42     | ✅        |\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Forest plot 新增 Claude-3.5 formality 行，3 judges CI 全部排除 0.50，点估计 0.62–0.665 密集分布\"\n    analysis: >\n      第 3 judge 方向一致 → C1 scope 可从 \"two judges\" 小幅升级为 \"across three judges on formality\"，\n      但仅 1 axis 覆盖不构成 full cross-judge validation。Reviewer 大概率认可方向一致性但\n      不会因此提高 novelty 评分。对 Findings 评分的边际贡献约 +0.1 分（从 3.0 到 3.1）。\n\n  - name: \"Multi-benchmark formality pairwise (not executed)\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-002\"\n    description: >\n      需要为 AlpacaEval/MT-Bench source texts 重新生成 counterfactuals（GPU 4h + API），\n      再在 3 judges 上 scoring（~$60-90）。exp-001 仅部分完成 + exp-020 消耗剩余预算后，\n      本实验无法启动。\n    expected_results:\n      status: \"not_executed\"\n      blocking_reason: \"API budget exhausted ($32 on exp-001 + ~$20 on exp-020); new CF generation requires additional GPU + API\"\n      cf_generation_started: false\n      paper_mitigation: \"Limitations section: 'Results demonstrated on LLMBar; benchmark generalization is future work.'\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Median 档核心假设之一是 \"multi-judge 扩展不足\"。Multi-benchmark 比 multi-judge 更资源密集\n      （需要全新 CF generation pipeline 运行），在 exp-001 已消耗主要 API 预算的前提下不可能执行。\n      这是 Findings vs Main 的关键差异：Main 需要 benchmark generalization，Findings 接受\n      single-benchmark deep analysis。论文需明确 acknowledge 但不影响 3.0–3.5 评分。\n    tables: []\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: >\n      Benchmark generalization 缺失是 median 档 Findings 定位的必然结果，不是失误。\n      Reviewer 会列为 limitation 但不会因此 reject Findings-track submission。\n\n  - name: \"Likert vs Pairwise sensitivity analysis (partial — 2 full + 1 partial judge)\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-003\"\n    description: >\n      基于 exp-001/exp-020 数据，整合 3 judges × formality + 2 judges × (verbosity, register) \n      的 Likert vs pairwise sensitivity 系统比较。7 个 available cells 的统一 sensitivity 分析。\n    expected_results:\n      formality_blindspot_confirmed: \"3/3 judges (GPT-4o, Qwen3-32B, Claude-3.5)\"\n      verbosity_blindspot_confirmed: \"2/2 judges (GPT-4o, Qwen3-32B)\"\n      register_blindspot_confirmed: \"1/2 (Qwen GEE sig → Blindspot; GPT-4o pairwise NS → unclassifiable)\"\n      overall_blindspot_rate: 0.86\n      avg_likert_tie_rate_across_cells: 0.66\n      likert_tie_rate_range: [0.58, 0.73]\n      sensitivity_gap_min: \"Likert p=0.179 vs pairwise p<0.0001 (Qwen verbosity)\"\n      sensitivity_gap_max: \"Likert p=0.908 vs pairwise p<0.0001 (Qwen formality)\"\n      power_deficit_likert: \"Mean effective n after ties = 34.7 (out of 100), vs pairwise effective n = 100\"\n      meta_analytic_pairwise_mean_bt: 0.67\n    result_rationale: >\n      Blindspot confirmation rate 0.86 (6/7 cells) 处于 tier 定义 [0.67, 0.83] 的略上方，\n      但若仅计 2 primary judges 的 6 cells → 5/6 = 0.83 精确命中上限。\n      第 7 个 cell（Claude formality）提供额外 confirmation 但不改变 primary 计数。\n      Likert tie rate 稳定在 0.58–0.73 横跨所有 judges 和 axes，这是 Blindspot 的 structural \n      根源：≥58% 的 Likert pairs 产生 ties，等效于将 n=100 降至 n~35 的有效样本量，\n      解释了为何 moderate effect (BT 63–77%) 在 Likert 上 undetectable。\n      这个 \"effective sample size\" 论证比单纯比较 p-values 更有力，因为它提供了 mechanistic explanation。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Complete Likert vs Pairwise detection matrix\"\n        content: |\n          | Judge       | Axis       | BT P(win) | BT p     | Likert ATE | Likert p | Tie Rate | Blindspot |\n          |------------|-----------|-----------|----------|------------|----------|----------|-----------|\n          | GPT-4o      | Formality  | 0.630     | <0.001   | ~0.08      | 0.332    | 0.625    | ✅        |\n          | GPT-4o      | Verbosity  | ~0.780    | <10⁻⁶   | -0.12      | 0.22     | 0.61     | ✅        |\n          | GPT-4o      | Register   | 0.580     | 0.085    | 0.05       | 0.55     | 0.65     | ⬜        |\n          | Qwen3-32B   | Formality  | 0.665     | <0.0001  | 0.011      | 0.908    | 0.727    | ✅        |\n          | Qwen3-32B   | Verbosity  | 0.773     | <0.0001  | -0.151     | 0.179    | 0.581    | ✅        |\n          | Qwen3-32B   | Register   | GEE 1.91  | 0.046    | 0.074      | 0.505    | 0.638    | ✅*       |\n          | Claude-3.5  | Formality  | 0.620     | 0.005    | 0.03       | 0.42     | 0.68     | ✅        |\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Paired dot plot: 每个 cell 一组，左点 Likert p 右点 pairwise p，连线。6/7 连线从右上(NS)到左下(sig)，视觉冲击力强\"\n    analysis: >\n      C2 的最强版本表述：\"Across 7 judge×axis cells with available data, Likert scoring failed \n      to reach significance in all 7 cases (p range: 0.179–0.908), while pairwise comparison \n      detected significant style bias in 6/7 cells (p range: <10⁻⁶ to 0.005; register GPT-4o \n      marginal at p=0.085).\" 配合 tie rate mechanistic explanation → Findings 级 solid contribution。\n\n  - name: \"Pairwise RATE control (GPT-4o × LLMBar only)\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-005\"\n    description: >\n      GPT-4o 对 100 formality pairs 执行 RATE-style double-rewrite control：\n      将每个 original text 做 identity double-rewrite (same style)，然后 pairwise compare \n      original vs double-rewrite。量化 judge 对 original text 的 inherent preference baseline。\n      仅在 GPT-4o × LLMBar 上执行，未扩展到其他 judge × benchmark。\n    expected_results:\n      original_pairwise_win_rate: 0.57\n      original_wilson_ci: [0.47, 0.67]\n      original_sign_test_p: 0.16\n      original_bt_prob: 0.555\n      original_bt_ci: [0.48, 0.63]\n      original_bt_p: 0.12\n      original_likert_ate: 0.06\n      original_likert_p: 0.45\n      style_effect_vs_original: \"formal OR=2.21 p=0.010 >> original OR=1.82 p=0.052\"\n      extended_to_other_judges: false\n    result_rationale: >\n      exp-014 GEE 已独立估计 original preference OR=1.82 p=0.052（marginal）。直接 RATE control \n      测量同一 confound 的 raw magnitude：~57% 偏好 original，不显著。\n      这个结果与 exp-014 一致而非矛盾——original preference 存在但不足以解释 formal style effect。\n      关键论证链：(1) RATE control ~57% NS → original preference alone 不显著，\n      (2) GEE 同时建模两个效应 → formal OR=2.21 显著 after controlling original OR=1.82，\n      (3) direction subset 进一步确认：formal→casual 78.8% 但 casual→formal 54.5% → \n      originality confound 集中在 casual→formal direction，而 formal→casual 几乎是 pure style。\n      未扩展到其他 judge 是 median 档资源约束——论文用 GPT-4o 数据论证 confound 量级足够，\n      Qwen3-32B 的 GEE 已提供跨模型 decomposition evidence。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"RATE control vs style effect decomposition\"\n        content: |\n          | Effect Source         | Measure      | Estimate | 95% CI      | p     | Significant |\n          |----------------------|-------------|----------|-------------|-------|-------------|\n          | Formal style (BT)    | BT win prob  | 0.630    | [0.558, 0.703] | <0.001 | ✅ |\n          | Original pref (RATE) | BT win prob  | 0.555    | [0.480, 0.630] | 0.12   | ❌ |\n          | Formal style (GEE)   | OR           | 2.21     | [1.21, 4.04]   | 0.010  | ✅ |\n          | Original pref (GEE)  | OR           | 1.82     | [0.99, 3.32]   | 0.052  | ❌ (marginal) |\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: >\n      RATE control 提供直觉上简洁的论证：same sign test，original preference NS，style effect sig → \n      不可归因于 original preference。与 GEE decomposition 互为补充。\n      Reviewer 可能追问 \"what if original preference varies by judge?\"——这是 not extending 的风险，\n      但 Findings 标准下 GPT-4o single-judge control + Qwen GEE 跨模型 decomposition 足够。\n\n  - name: \"Scaled replication n=300-500 (not executed)\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-006\"\n    description: >\n      将 formality 实验从 n=100 扩展到 n=300-500 的 large-scale replication 未执行。\n      前置依赖 exp-001/002 未充分完成，且预算优先分配给 exp-020 完成证据矩阵。\n    expected_results:\n      status: \"not_executed\"\n      blocking_reason: \"Budget prioritized for 2×3 matrix completion (exp-020) and 3rd judge (exp-001)\"\n      adequacy_argument: \"Current n=100 → BT CI width ~15pp, all primary cells exclude 0.50\"\n      power_curve_argument: \"BT at n=100 has >95% power for effects ≥0.63; scaling adds precision not detection\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Median 档的 resource allocation 逻辑：breadth (更多 cells/judges) 优于 depth (单 cell 更大 n)。\n      当前 n=100 的 BT 对所有 primary cells 已有足够 power：\n      - formality GPT-4o BT 63% CI [55.8, 70.3] → CI width 14.5pp, excludes 50%\n      - Qwen verbosity BT 77.3% CI [70.3, 84.3] → CI width 14pp, excludes 50%\n      n=300 会将 CI 收窄到 ~8pp，提供更精确的 point estimate 但不改变 any conclusion。\n      这对 Findings 评审者的 marginal value 远低于完成 2×3 矩阵（exp-020）或新增第 3 judge（exp-001）。\n      论文中 power curve figure 已论证 n=100 的 adequacy——这个 figure 的存在本身就是对 \n      \"why not larger n\" 的 preemptive answer。\n    tables: []\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: >\n      不执行对评分无实质影响。如果 reviewer 提出 \"small n\" concern，power curve + existing CI \n      足以回应。真正的 scaling need 是 multi-benchmark（exp-002）而非 single-benchmark larger n。\n\n  - name: \"Register axis GPT-4o scoring (via exp-020)\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-008\"\n    description: >\n      GPT-4o 对 94 个 NLI-verified register counterfactual pairs 执行 pairwise + Likert scoring。\n      CF verification 已完成（94% NLI pass）。与 exp-020 合并执行以节省 API 调用开销。\n      Qwen3-32B register scoring 已在 exp-019 完成。\n    expected_results:\n      gpt4o_register_bt_win_prob: 0.58\n      gpt4o_register_bt_ci: [0.50, 0.66]\n      gpt4o_register_bt_p: 0.085\n      gpt4o_register_likert_ate: 0.05\n      gpt4o_register_likert_p: 0.55\n      gpt4o_register_likert_tie_rate: 0.65\n      gpt4o_register_consistency_rate: 0.55\n      gpt4o_register_gee_academic_or: 1.75\n      gpt4o_register_gee_academic_p: 0.08\n      gpt4o_register_gee_originality_or: 3.50\n      gpt4o_register_gee_originality_p: 0.002\n      cross_judge_pattern: \"Both GPT-4o and Qwen3-32B show originality-dominated register axis\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      GPT-4o register pairwise 63.3% p=0.085 已在早期实验中观察到（sign test on consistent pairs）。\n      BT 模型纳入 position-inconsistent pairs 后 point estimate 会下降至 ~58%，CI 可能包含 0.50。\n      这与 GPT-4o 整体偏低的 style sensitivity 一致（formality BT 63% 也是 3 judges 中最低）。\n      GEE decomposition 预期复制 Qwen3-32B 的 originality-dominated pattern：\n      academic style OR ~1.75 (NS at p~0.08) vs originality OR ~3.50 (sig at p=0.002)。\n      GPT-4o 的 originality OR (3.50) 低于 Qwen (5.72) 是因为 GPT-4o 对 content quality \n      差异的 sensitivity 也弱于 Qwen（与 formality 的 cross-judge pattern 一致）。\n      Register 在 GPT-4o 上 style effect 不显著 → 这个 cell 不构成经典 Blindspot \n      （pairwise 本身 NS，Likert NS 是 expected null）。\n      但 GEE 揭示 originality confound 掩盖了 marginal style effect → 支持 C3 gradient narrative。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Register GEE cross-judge decomposition\"\n        content: |\n          | Judge       | Academic OR | p     | Originality OR | p       | Ratio Orig/Style | Classification       |\n          |------------|-----------|-------|---------------|---------|-----------------|---------------------|\n          | Qwen3-32B   | 1.91      | 0.046 | 5.72          | <0.0001 | 3.0×            | Originality-dominated |\n          | GPT-4o      | 1.75      | 0.08  | 3.50          | 0.002   | 2.0×            | Originality-dominated |\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Forest plot register row: 两个 judge BT CI 均触及或跨越 0.50 虚线，与 formality/verbosity 的清晰分离形成视觉对比\"\n    analysis: >\n      Register 在两个 judge 上一致 originality-dominated → C3 GEE gradient 右端点稳定。\n      论文定位：register 不是 \"failed detection\"，而是 \"method boundary illustration\"——\n      当 axis 改变的不只是 surface style 时，content change dominates and pairwise signal is diluted。\n      这给 practitioner 的 actionable insight：对 register-like axes 需要更强的 content control \n      或不同的 measurement strategy。\n\n  - name: \"Non-Qwen rewriter control (not executed)\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-009\"\n    description: >\n      使用 Llama-3.1-70B 或 Mistral 作为替代 rewriter 的控制实验。P2 优先级，\n      需 8h GPU + API 预算，在 P0/P1 实验完成后资源不足。\n    expected_results:\n      status: \"not_executed\"\n      blocking_reason: \"P2 priority; GPU budget (8h) and API budget consumed by P0/P1 experiments\"\n      indirect_evidence: >\n        Cross-judge consistency (GPT-4o proprietary ≠ Qwen3-32B open-source, same direction) \n        provides partial mitigation — if CFs had Qwen-specific artifacts, different-family judges \n        would respond differently.\n      paper_mitigation: \"Limitations section acknowledges single-rewriter setup; NLI gate is model-agnostic\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Median 档的 P2 实验预期不执行。资源分配逻辑：\n      (1) exp-001 ($32) + exp-020 (~$20) + exp-005 (~$15) 已消耗约 $67 API 预算\n      (2) GPU 时间分配给 Qwen3-32B local scoring (exp-017/018/019 ~6h) \n      (3) 剩余 GPU/API 不足以支持 8h Llama-3.1-70B rewriting + verification\n      论文通过三层间接论证 mitigate：\n      (a) NLI verification 是 model-agnostic 质量门控（exp-013 precision 98.9%）\n      (b) 两个不同架构/训练的 judge 对相同 CFs 反应一致\n      (c) Formality CFs 的 direction-aware analysis 排除了 systematic rewriting direction bias\n      Reviewer 可能列为 weakness 但不 deal-breaking for Findings。\n    tables: []\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: >\n      如果 reviewer 强烈要求，可在 camera-ready revision 阶段用 Llama-3.1 做 quick pilot\n      （n=20 formality, ~2h GPU）。Median 档预期不需要——Findings 级别对 robustness check \n      的要求低于 Main。\n\n  - name: \"GPT-4o verbosity + register scoring (completes 2×3 evidence matrix)\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-020\"\n    description: >\n      GPT-4o API 对 verbosity 100 pairs 和 register 94 pairs 执行完整 Likert + pairwise scoring。\n      关键缺失数据：GPT-4o verbosity Likert ATE（确认 6th Blindspot cell）。\n      Register 数据在 exp-008 中合并报告。本条目聚焦 verbosity 新增数据。\n    expected_results:\n      # Verbosity (primary — the key missing piece)\n      gpt4o_verbosity_bt_win_prob: 0.78\n      gpt4o_verbosity_bt_ci: [0.70, 0.85]\n      gpt4o_verbosity_bt_p: \"<10⁻⁶\"\n      gpt4o_verbosity_pairwise_raw_win_rate: 0.863\n      gpt4o_verbosity_likert_ate: -0.12\n      gpt4o_verbosity_likert_p: 0.22\n      gpt4o_verbosity_likert_cohens_d: -0.11\n      gpt4o_verbosity_likert_tie_rate: 0.61\n      gpt4o_verbosity_blindspot_confirmed: true\n      gpt4o_verbosity_gee_verbose_or: 10.5\n      gpt4o_verbosity_gee_verbose_ci: [4.2, 26.3]\n      gpt4o_verbosity_gee_verbose_p: \"<10⁻⁷\"\n      gpt4o_verbosity_gee_originality_or: 0.55\n      gpt4o_verbosity_gee_originality_ci: [0.22, 1.38]\n      gpt4o_verbosity_gee_originality_p: 0.15\n      # Register (see exp-008 for details)\n      gpt4o_register_bt_win_prob: 0.58\n      gpt4o_register_bt_p: 0.085\n      # Matrix completion summary\n      evidence_matrix_cells_with_data: 6\n      blindspot_confirmed_cells: 5\n      blindspot_note: \"Register GPT-4o pairwise NS → 5th cell unclassifiable as Blindspot but GEE reveals masked style effect\"\n      total_api_cost: \"$19\"\n      # Final tier-level aggregate metrics\n      bt_win_prob_range_primary: [0.58, 0.78]\n      likert_tie_rate_mean: 0.66\n      gee_gradient_confirmed_cross_judge: true\n    result_rationale: >\n      **GPT-4o verbosity Likert ATE NS (p=0.22)** 是 median 档最关键的单一预测。推导逻辑：\n      \n      (1) Qwen3-32B verbosity Likert ATE=-0.151 p=0.179，效应方向为 negative（verbose 得分反而略低），\n      Cohen's d=-0.146。GPT-4o 预期同模式：Likert 尺度上 verbose 和 concise 得分几乎无差异，\n      因为 Likert absolute scoring 对 \"哪个更好\" 的判断被 variance within score level 淹没。\n      \n      (2) Tie rate ~61% 意味着有效样本量 n_eff ≈ 39。在 d=0.11 的效应下，\n      需要 n>500 才有 80% power 检测——当前 n=100 (n_eff≈39) 严重 underpowered。\n      这与 power curve figure 的论证完全吻合。\n      \n      (3) GPT-4o verbosity pairwise 86.3% 是全矩阵最强信号，但 Likert p=0.22 → \n      这是 Blindspot 的 most dramatic demonstration：最大的 style bias 在 Likert 上完全不可见。\n      这个对比将成为 abstract/intro 的 headline result。\n      \n      (4) GEE decomposition 预期复制 Qwen3-32B 的 pure style pattern：verbose OR ~10.5 \n      (略低于 Qwen 13.10，因为 GPT-4o style sensitivity 系统性弱于 Qwen)，\n      originality OR ~0.55 NS（方向一致——concise text 不因 content 被偏好，bias 完全来自 verbose style）。\n      Cross-judge GEE gradient 一致：verbosity pure style > formality mixed > register originality-dominated。\n      \n      (5) API cost ~$19 可控（200 verbosity pairwise + 200 Likert + 188 register pairwise + 188 register Likert\n      ≈ 776 API calls × ~$0.025/call）。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Complete 2×3 Evidence Matrix (median tier final)\"\n        content: |\n          |            | GPT-4o BT [CI]              | GPT-4o Likert p | Qwen3-32B BT [CI]           | Qwen3-32B Likert p | Blindspot |\n          |-----------|---------------------------|-----------------|---------------------------|-------------------|-----------|\n          | Formality  | 63.0% [55.8, 70.3]***      | 0.332           | 66.5% [58.5, 73.9]****     | 0.908             | 2/2 ✅    |\n          | Verbosity  | 78.0% [70.0, 85.0]****     | 0.22            | 77.3% [70.3, 84.3]****     | 0.179             | 2/2 ✅    |\n          | Register   | 58.0% [50.0, 66.0] (NS)    | 0.55            | GEE OR=1.91 [1.01, 3.58]*  | 0.505             | 1/2 ✅    |\n      - name: \"Cross-judge GEE gradient (complete)\"\n        content: |\n          | Axis       | Judge     | Style OR | Style p  | Origin. OR | Origin. p | Classification       |\n          |-----------|----------|---------|----------|-----------|----------|---------------------|\n          | Verbosity  | Qwen3-32B | 13.10   | <10⁻⁹   | 0.49 (NS) | 0.096    | Pure style           |\n          | Verbosity  | GPT-4o    | 10.50   | <10⁻⁷   | 0.55 (NS) | 0.15     | Pure style           |\n          | Formality  | Qwen3-32B | 4.20    | 0.0002   | 4.70      | <0.0001  | Mixed                |\n          | Formality  | GPT-4o    | 2.21    | 0.010    | 1.82      | 0.052    | Mixed (marginal)     |\n          | Register   | Qwen3-32B | 1.91    | 0.046    | 5.72      | <0.0001  | Originality-dominated |\n          | Register   | GPT-4o    | 1.75    | 0.08     | 3.50      | 0.002    | Originality-dominated |\n    figures_description:\n      - >\n        Forest plot (Figure 3, final): 6 rows (2 judges × 3 axes), x-axis = BT win probability,\n        dashed line at 0.50. Verbosity cells 最右 (0.77–0.78), formality 中间 (0.62–0.665),\n        register 接近 0.50 (0.58). 视觉上清晰分离三档。\n      - >\n        GEE gradient scatter: x = style OR (log scale), y = originality OR (log scale),\n        6 points 按 axis 着色 (verbosity 蓝, formality 绿, register 红), 按 judge 标记 (圆/方)。\n        Verbosity 右下角 (high style, low originality), register 左上角 (low style, high originality),\n        formality 对角线上 (both moderate)。两个 judge 的同轴点紧密聚类 → cross-judge consistency。\n    analysis: >\n      exp-020 完成后，median 档的证据结构完整：\n      - C1: CSD pipeline detects style bias across 2 judges × 3 axes (5/6 primary cells significant)\n      - C2: Likert Blindspot confirmed in 5/6 cells; mechanism = tie-induced power deficit\n      - C3: GEE gradient consistent across judges — verbosity pure → formality mixed → register originality-dominated\n      - C4: Practitioner guidance grounded in complete 2×3 matrix\n      \n      Forest plot + GEE gradient visualization 构成两个 key figures，配合 power curve (Figure 1) \n      和 pipeline diagram (Figure 2) = 4 figures total（比 planned 3 多 1，但 GEE scatter \n      可以 inline 在 results section 不占 figure slot）。\n      \n      Expected review score 3.0–3.5 的支撑：\n      - Evidence depth: 2×3 matrix complete, BT + GEE + ordinal regression, NLI validation\n      - Writing quality: 3 figures (power curve + pipeline + forest plot), ≤8.5 pages, 22+ refs\n      - Novelty cap: Likert Blindspot is domain transfer of known psychometric phenomenon → Findings\n      - Risk: new reviewer scores novelty ≤2.5 → need writing + evidence to compensate to 3.0 floor\n```"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":22645,"cache_read_input_tokens":11841,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":22645},"output_tokens":26,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"fe4f732d-0abd-4b87-8c2d-8b5d94071a71","uuid":"ceae7dea-304a-4241-ad61-5f4c682d5fd4"}
{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"api_error_status":null,"duration_ms":412666,"duration_api_ms":414312,"num_turns":1,"result":"```yaml\ntier: median\nnarrative_guidance: >\n  C1/C2 在 2 judges 范围内成立，claims 加 scope qualifier \"across the two judges tested\"。\n  C3 GEE gradient 定位为 empirical finding 非 generalizable insight。\n  Register 降为 method boundary case study。Blindspot 定位为 \"measurement sensitivity gap \n  documented in controlled setting\"。第 3 judge 仅覆盖 formality 1 axis，提供方向确认但不够升级 scope。\n  Findings 3.0–3.5 稳定落位。\n\nimagined_experiments:\n  - name: \"Multi-judge formality pairwise (partial — 1/2 judges completed)\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-001\"\n    description: >\n      Claude-3.5-Sonnet 完成 formality pairwise+Likert scoring（100 pairs × 2 directions）。\n      Gemini-2.0-Flash 因 API 额度耗尽仅完成 ~40% calls，数据不足以纳入正式分析。\n      最终仅新增 1 个 judge 的 formality 完整数据。\n    expected_results:\n      claude_bt_win_prob: 0.62\n      claude_bt_ci: [0.54, 0.70]\n      claude_bt_p: 0.005\n      claude_likert_ate: 0.03\n      claude_likert_p: 0.42\n      claude_likert_tie_rate: 0.68\n      claude_likert_cohens_d: 0.03\n      claude_consistency_rate: 0.58\n      claude_blindspot_confirmed: true\n      claude_gee_formal_or: 2.80\n      claude_gee_formal_p: 0.006\n      claude_gee_originality_or: 2.10\n      claude_gee_originality_p: 0.03\n      gemini_status: \"incomplete (~80/200 pairwise calls, excluded from analysis)\"\n      gemini_partial_formal_win_trend: \"~64% on available data, consistent direction\"\n      total_api_spend: \"$32 (Claude $22 + Gemini partial $10)\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Claude-3.5-Sonnet 作为 Anthropic proprietary model，style sensitivity 预期介于 GPT-4o (63.0%)\n      和 Qwen3-32B (66.5%) 之间偏低端。原因：(1) Claude 系列以 \"helpful, harmless\" 训练，对 style \n      的 systematic preference 可能弱于 Qwen 的 RLHF-heavy 训练，(2) BT 0.62 处于 tier 定义的\n      [0.58, 0.78] 区间下端，反映 \"方向确认但非最强信号\"。\n      Likert ATE NS (p=0.42) 延续 Blindspot pattern：tie rate ~68% 与其他 judge 一致（GPT-4o 62.5%,\n      Qwen 72.7%），表明 Likert insensitivity 是 measurement structure 问题而非 judge-specific。\n      GEE decomposition 显示 formality-originality mixed pattern（与 GPT-4o/Qwen 同方向），\n      OR 值略高于 GPT-4o (2.21) 但低于 Qwen (4.20)——不同 judge 内部权重分配不同但 pattern 一致。\n      Gemini 不完整是典型 median 档资源约束：~$30/judge × 2 judges 超出实际可用 API 预算弹性，\n      第二个 judge 被 cut。论文只能脚注提及 \"partial directional evidence from a third judge\"。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Cross-judge formality BT summary\"\n        content: |\n          | Judge        | BT P(formal) | 95% CI        | p       | Likert ATE | Likert p | Blindspot |\n          |-------------|-------------|---------------|---------|------------|----------|-----------|\n          | GPT-4o       | 0.630       | [0.558, 0.703] | <0.001  | ~0.08      | 0.332    | ✅        |\n          | Qwen3-32B    | 0.665       | [0.585, 0.739] | <0.0001 | 0.011      | 0.908    | ✅        |\n          | Claude-3.5   | 0.620       | [0.540, 0.700] | 0.005   | 0.03       | 0.42     | ✅        |\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Forest plot 新增 Claude-3.5 formality 行，3 judges CI 全部排除 0.50，点估计 0.62–0.665 密集分布\"\n    analysis: >\n      第 3 judge 方向一致 → C1 scope 可从 \"two judges\" 小幅升级为 \"across three judges on formality\"，\n      但仅 1 axis 覆盖不构成 full cross-judge validation。Reviewer 大概率认可方向一致性但\n      不会因此提高 novelty 评分。对 Findings 评分的边际贡献约 +0.1 分（从 3.0 到 3.1）。\n\n  - name: \"Multi-benchmark formality pairwise (not executed)\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-002\"\n    description: >\n      需要为 AlpacaEval/MT-Bench source texts 重新生成 counterfactuals（GPU 4h + API），\n      再在 3 judges 上 scoring（~$60-90）。exp-001 仅部分完成 + exp-020 消耗剩余预算后，\n      本实验无法启动。\n    expected_results:\n      status: \"not_executed\"\n      blocking_reason: \"API budget exhausted ($32 on exp-001 + ~$20 on exp-020); new CF generation requires additional GPU + API\"\n      cf_generation_started: false\n      paper_mitigation: \"Limitations section: 'Results demonstrated on LLMBar; benchmark generalization is future work.'\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Median 档核心假设之一是 \"multi-judge 扩展不足\"。Multi-benchmark 比 multi-judge 更资源密集\n      （需要全新 CF generation pipeline 运行），在 exp-001 已消耗主要 API 预算的前提下不可能执行。\n      这是 Findings vs Main 的关键差异：Main 需要 benchmark generalization，Findings 接受\n      single-benchmark deep analysis。论文需明确 acknowledge 但不影响 3.0–3.5 评分。\n    tables: []\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: >\n      Benchmark generalization 缺失是 median 档 Findings 定位的必然结果，不是失误。\n      Reviewer 会列为 limitation 但不会因此 reject Findings-track submission。\n\n  - name: \"Likert vs Pairwise sensitivity analysis (partial — 2 full + 1 partial judge)\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-003\"\n    description: >\n      基于 exp-001/exp-020 数据，整合 3 judges × formality + 2 judges × (verbosity, register) \n      的 Likert vs pairwise sensitivity 系统比较。7 个 available cells 的统一 sensitivity 分析。\n    expected_results:\n      formality_blindspot_confirmed: \"3/3 judges (GPT-4o, Qwen3-32B, Claude-3.5)\"\n      verbosity_blindspot_confirmed: \"2/2 judges (GPT-4o, Qwen3-32B)\"\n      register_blindspot_confirmed: \"1/2 (Qwen GEE sig → Blindspot; GPT-4o pairwise NS → unclassifiable)\"\n      overall_blindspot_rate: 0.86\n      avg_likert_tie_rate_across_cells: 0.66\n      likert_tie_rate_range: [0.58, 0.73]\n      sensitivity_gap_min: \"Likert p=0.179 vs pairwise p<0.0001 (Qwen verbosity)\"\n      sensitivity_gap_max: \"Likert p=0.908 vs pairwise p<0.0001 (Qwen formality)\"\n      power_deficit_likert: \"Mean effective n after ties = 34.7 (out of 100), vs pairwise effective n = 100\"\n      meta_analytic_pairwise_mean_bt: 0.67\n    result_rationale: >\n      Blindspot confirmation rate 0.86 (6/7 cells) 处于 tier 定义 [0.67, 0.83] 的略上方，\n      但若仅计 2 primary judges 的 6 cells → 5/6 = 0.83 精确命中上限。\n      第 7 个 cell（Claude formality）提供额外 confirmation 但不改变 primary 计数。\n      Likert tie rate 稳定在 0.58–0.73 横跨所有 judges 和 axes，这是 Blindspot 的 structural \n      根源：≥58% 的 Likert pairs 产生 ties，等效于将 n=100 降至 n~35 的有效样本量，\n      解释了为何 moderate effect (BT 63–77%) 在 Likert 上 undetectable。\n      这个 \"effective sample size\" 论证比单纯比较 p-values 更有力，因为它提供了 mechanistic explanation。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Complete Likert vs Pairwise detection matrix\"\n        content: |\n          | Judge       | Axis       | BT P(win) | BT p     | Likert ATE | Likert p | Tie Rate | Blindspot |\n          |------------|-----------|-----------|----------|------------|----------|----------|-----------|\n          | GPT-4o      | Formality  | 0.630     | <0.001   | ~0.08      | 0.332    | 0.625    | ✅        |\n          | GPT-4o      | Verbosity  | ~0.780    | <10⁻⁶   | -0.12      | 0.22     | 0.61     | ✅        |\n          | GPT-4o      | Register   | 0.580     | 0.085    | 0.05       | 0.55     | 0.65     | ⬜        |\n          | Qwen3-32B   | Formality  | 0.665     | <0.0001  | 0.011      | 0.908    | 0.727    | ✅        |\n          | Qwen3-32B   | Verbosity  | 0.773     | <0.0001  | -0.151     | 0.179    | 0.581    | ✅        |\n          | Qwen3-32B   | Register   | GEE 1.91  | 0.046    | 0.074      | 0.505    | 0.638    | ✅*       |\n          | Claude-3.5  | Formality  | 0.620     | 0.005    | 0.03       | 0.42     | 0.68     | ✅        |\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Paired dot plot: 每个 cell 一组，左点 Likert p 右点 pairwise p，连线。6/7 连线从右上(NS)到左下(sig)，视觉冲击力强\"\n    analysis: >\n      C2 的最强版本表述：\"Across 7 judge×axis cells with available data, Likert scoring failed \n      to reach significance in all 7 cases (p range: 0.179–0.908), while pairwise comparison \n      detected significant style bias in 6/7 cells (p range: <10⁻⁶ to 0.005; register GPT-4o \n      marginal at p=0.085).\" 配合 tie rate mechanistic explanation → Findings 级 solid contribution。\n\n  - name: \"Pairwise RATE control (GPT-4o × LLMBar only)\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-005\"\n    description: >\n      GPT-4o 对 100 formality pairs 执行 RATE-style double-rewrite control：\n      将每个 original text 做 identity double-rewrite (same style)，然后 pairwise compare \n      original vs double-rewrite。量化 judge 对 original text 的 inherent preference baseline。\n      仅在 GPT-4o × LLMBar 上执行，未扩展到其他 judge × benchmark。\n    expected_results:\n      original_pairwise_win_rate: 0.57\n      original_wilson_ci: [0.47, 0.67]\n      original_sign_test_p: 0.16\n      original_bt_prob: 0.555\n      original_bt_ci: [0.48, 0.63]\n      original_bt_p: 0.12\n      original_likert_ate: 0.06\n      original_likert_p: 0.45\n      style_effect_vs_original: \"formal OR=2.21 p=0.010 >> original OR=1.82 p=0.052\"\n      extended_to_other_judges: false\n    result_rationale: >\n      exp-014 GEE 已独立估计 original preference OR=1.82 p=0.052（marginal）。直接 RATE control \n      测量同一 confound 的 raw magnitude：~57% 偏好 original，不显著。\n      这个结果与 exp-014 一致而非矛盾——original preference 存在但不足以解释 formal style effect。\n      关键论证链：(1) RATE control ~57% NS → original preference alone 不显著，\n      (2) GEE 同时建模两个效应 → formal OR=2.21 显著 after controlling original OR=1.82，\n      (3) direction subset 进一步确认：formal→casual 78.8% 但 casual→formal 54.5% → \n      originality confound 集中在 casual→formal direction，而 formal→casual 几乎是 pure style。\n      未扩展到其他 judge 是 median 档资源约束——论文用 GPT-4o 数据论证 confound 量级足够，\n      Qwen3-32B 的 GEE 已提供跨模型 decomposition evidence。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"RATE control vs style effect decomposition\"\n        content: |\n          | Effect Source         | Measure      | Estimate | 95% CI      | p     | Significant |\n          |----------------------|-------------|----------|-------------|-------|-------------|\n          | Formal style (BT)    | BT win prob  | 0.630    | [0.558, 0.703] | <0.001 | ✅ |\n          | Original pref (RATE) | BT win prob  | 0.555    | [0.480, 0.630] | 0.12   | ❌ |\n          | Formal style (GEE)   | OR           | 2.21     | [1.21, 4.04]   | 0.010  | ✅ |\n          | Original pref (GEE)  | OR           | 1.82     | [0.99, 3.32]   | 0.052  | ❌ (marginal) |\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: >\n      RATE control 提供直觉上简洁的论证：same sign test，original preference NS，style effect sig → \n      不可归因于 original preference。与 GEE decomposition 互为补充。\n      Reviewer 可能追问 \"what if original preference varies by judge?\"——这是 not extending 的风险，\n      但 Findings 标准下 GPT-4o single-judge control + Qwen GEE 跨模型 decomposition 足够。\n\n  - name: \"Scaled replication n=300-500 (not executed)\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-006\"\n    description: >\n      将 formality 实验从 n=100 扩展到 n=300-500 的 large-scale replication 未执行。\n      前置依赖 exp-001/002 未充分完成，且预算优先分配给 exp-020 完成证据矩阵。\n    expected_results:\n      status: \"not_executed\"\n      blocking_reason: \"Budget prioritized for 2×3 matrix completion (exp-020) and 3rd judge (exp-001)\"\n      adequacy_argument: \"Current n=100 → BT CI width ~15pp, all primary cells exclude 0.50\"\n      power_curve_argument: \"BT at n=100 has >95% power for effects ≥0.63; scaling adds precision not detection\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Median 档的 resource allocation 逻辑：breadth (更多 cells/judges) 优于 depth (单 cell 更大 n)。\n      当前 n=100 的 BT 对所有 primary cells 已有足够 power：\n      - formality GPT-4o BT 63% CI [55.8, 70.3] → CI width 14.5pp, excludes 50%\n      - Qwen verbosity BT 77.3% CI [70.3, 84.3] → CI width 14pp, excludes 50%\n      n=300 会将 CI 收窄到 ~8pp，提供更精确的 point estimate 但不改变 any conclusion。\n      这对 Findings 评审者的 marginal value 远低于完成 2×3 矩阵（exp-020）或新增第 3 judge（exp-001）。\n      论文中 power curve figure 已论证 n=100 的 adequacy——这个 figure 的存在本身就是对 \n      \"why not larger n\" 的 preemptive answer。\n    tables: []\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: >\n      不执行对评分无实质影响。如果 reviewer 提出 \"small n\" concern，power curve + existing CI \n      足以回应。真正的 scaling need 是 multi-benchmark（exp-002）而非 single-benchmark larger n。\n\n  - name: \"Register axis GPT-4o scoring (via exp-020)\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-008\"\n    description: >\n      GPT-4o 对 94 个 NLI-verified register counterfactual pairs 执行 pairwise + Likert scoring。\n      CF verification 已完成（94% NLI pass）。与 exp-020 合并执行以节省 API 调用开销。\n      Qwen3-32B register scoring 已在 exp-019 完成。\n    expected_results:\n      gpt4o_register_bt_win_prob: 0.58\n      gpt4o_register_bt_ci: [0.50, 0.66]\n      gpt4o_register_bt_p: 0.085\n      gpt4o_register_likert_ate: 0.05\n      gpt4o_register_likert_p: 0.55\n      gpt4o_register_likert_tie_rate: 0.65\n      gpt4o_register_consistency_rate: 0.55\n      gpt4o_register_gee_academic_or: 1.75\n      gpt4o_register_gee_academic_p: 0.08\n      gpt4o_register_gee_originality_or: 3.50\n      gpt4o_register_gee_originality_p: 0.002\n      cross_judge_pattern: \"Both GPT-4o and Qwen3-32B show originality-dominated register axis\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      GPT-4o register pairwise 63.3% p=0.085 已在早期实验中观察到（sign test on consistent pairs）。\n      BT 模型纳入 position-inconsistent pairs 后 point estimate 会下降至 ~58%，CI 可能包含 0.50。\n      这与 GPT-4o 整体偏低的 style sensitivity 一致（formality BT 63% 也是 3 judges 中最低）。\n      GEE decomposition 预期复制 Qwen3-32B 的 originality-dominated pattern：\n      academic style OR ~1.75 (NS at p~0.08) vs originality OR ~3.50 (sig at p=0.002)。\n      GPT-4o 的 originality OR (3.50) 低于 Qwen (5.72) 是因为 GPT-4o 对 content quality \n      差异的 sensitivity 也弱于 Qwen（与 formality 的 cross-judge pattern 一致）。\n      Register 在 GPT-4o 上 style effect 不显著 → 这个 cell 不构成经典 Blindspot \n      （pairwise 本身 NS，Likert NS 是 expected null）。\n      但 GEE 揭示 originality confound 掩盖了 marginal style effect → 支持 C3 gradient narrative。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Register GEE cross-judge decomposition\"\n        content: |\n          | Judge       | Academic OR | p     | Originality OR | p       | Ratio Orig/Style | Classification       |\n          |------------|-----------|-------|---------------|---------|-----------------|---------------------|\n          | Qwen3-32B   | 1.91      | 0.046 | 5.72          | <0.0001 | 3.0×            | Originality-dominated |\n          | GPT-4o      | 1.75      | 0.08  | 3.50          | 0.002   | 2.0×            | Originality-dominated |\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Forest plot register row: 两个 judge BT CI 均触及或跨越 0.50 虚线，与 formality/verbosity 的清晰分离形成视觉对比\"\n    analysis: >\n      Register 在两个 judge 上一致 originality-dominated → C3 GEE gradient 右端点稳定。\n      论文定位：register 不是 \"failed detection\"，而是 \"method boundary illustration\"——\n      当 axis 改变的不只是 surface style 时，content change dominates and pairwise signal is diluted。\n      这给 practitioner 的 actionable insight：对 register-like axes 需要更强的 content control \n      或不同的 measurement strategy。\n\n  - name: \"Non-Qwen rewriter control (not executed)\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-009\"\n    description: >\n      使用 Llama-3.1-70B 或 Mistral 作为替代 rewriter 的控制实验。P2 优先级，\n      需 8h GPU + API 预算，在 P0/P1 实验完成后资源不足。\n    expected_results:\n      status: \"not_executed\"\n      blocking_reason: \"P2 priority; GPU budget (8h) and API budget consumed by P0/P1 experiments\"\n      indirect_evidence: >\n        Cross-judge consistency (GPT-4o proprietary ≠ Qwen3-32B open-source, same direction) \n        provides partial mitigation — if CFs had Qwen-specific artifacts, different-family judges \n        would respond differently.\n      paper_mitigation: \"Limitations section acknowledges single-rewriter setup; NLI gate is model-agnostic\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Median 档的 P2 实验预期不执行。资源分配逻辑：\n      (1) exp-001 ($32) + exp-020 (~$20) + exp-005 (~$15) 已消耗约 $67 API 预算\n      (2) GPU 时间分配给 Qwen3-32B local scoring (exp-017/018/019 ~6h) \n      (3) 剩余 GPU/API 不足以支持 8h Llama-3.1-70B rewriting + verification\n      论文通过三层间接论证 mitigate：\n      (a) NLI verification 是 model-agnostic 质量门控（exp-013 precision 98.9%）\n      (b) 两个不同架构/训练的 judge 对相同 CFs 反应一致\n      (c) Formality CFs 的 direction-aware analysis 排除了 systematic rewriting direction bias\n      Reviewer 可能列为 weakness 但不 deal-breaking for Findings。\n    tables: []\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: >\n      如果 reviewer 强烈要求，可在 camera-ready revision 阶段用 Llama-3.1 做 quick pilot\n      （n=20 formality, ~2h GPU）。Median 档预期不需要——Findings 级别对 robustness check \n      的要求低于 Main。\n\n  - name: \"GPT-4o verbosity + register scoring (completes 2×3 evidence matrix)\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-020\"\n    description: >\n      GPT-4o API 对 verbosity 100 pairs 和 register 94 pairs 执行完整 Likert + pairwise scoring。\n      关键缺失数据：GPT-4o verbosity Likert ATE（确认 6th Blindspot cell）。\n      Register 数据在 exp-008 中合并报告。本条目聚焦 verbosity 新增数据。\n    expected_results:\n      # Verbosity (primary — the key missing piece)\n      gpt4o_verbosity_bt_win_prob: 0.78\n      gpt4o_verbosity_bt_ci: [0.70, 0.85]\n      gpt4o_verbosity_bt_p: \"<10⁻⁶\"\n      gpt4o_verbosity_pairwise_raw_win_rate: 0.863\n      gpt4o_verbosity_likert_ate: -0.12\n      gpt4o_verbosity_likert_p: 0.22\n      gpt4o_verbosity_likert_cohens_d: -0.11\n      gpt4o_verbosity_likert_tie_rate: 0.61\n      gpt4o_verbosity_blindspot_confirmed: true\n      gpt4o_verbosity_gee_verbose_or: 10.5\n      gpt4o_verbosity_gee_verbose_ci: [4.2, 26.3]\n      gpt4o_verbosity_gee_verbose_p: \"<10⁻⁷\"\n      gpt4o_verbosity_gee_originality_or: 0.55\n      gpt4o_verbosity_gee_originality_ci: [0.22, 1.38]\n      gpt4o_verbosity_gee_originality_p: 0.15\n      # Register (see exp-008 for details)\n      gpt4o_register_bt_win_prob: 0.58\n      gpt4o_register_bt_p: 0.085\n      # Matrix completion summary\n      evidence_matrix_cells_with_data: 6\n      blindspot_confirmed_cells: 5\n      blindspot_note: \"Register GPT-4o pairwise NS → 5th cell unclassifiable as Blindspot but GEE reveals masked style effect\"\n      total_api_cost: \"$19\"\n      # Final tier-level aggregate metrics\n      bt_win_prob_range_primary: [0.58, 0.78]\n      likert_tie_rate_mean: 0.66\n      gee_gradient_confirmed_cross_judge: true\n    result_rationale: >\n      **GPT-4o verbosity Likert ATE NS (p=0.22)** 是 median 档最关键的单一预测。推导逻辑：\n      \n      (1) Qwen3-32B verbosity Likert ATE=-0.151 p=0.179，效应方向为 negative（verbose 得分反而略低），\n      Cohen's d=-0.146。GPT-4o 预期同模式：Likert 尺度上 verbose 和 concise 得分几乎无差异，\n      因为 Likert absolute scoring 对 \"哪个更好\" 的判断被 variance within score level 淹没。\n      \n      (2) Tie rate ~61% 意味着有效样本量 n_eff ≈ 39。在 d=0.11 的效应下，\n      需要 n>500 才有 80% power 检测——当前 n=100 (n_eff≈39) 严重 underpowered。\n      这与 power curve figure 的论证完全吻合。\n      \n      (3) GPT-4o verbosity pairwise 86.3% 是全矩阵最强信号，但 Likert p=0.22 → \n      这是 Blindspot 的 most dramatic demonstration：最大的 style bias 在 Likert 上完全不可见。\n      这个对比将成为 abstract/intro 的 headline result。\n      \n      (4) GEE decomposition 预期复制 Qwen3-32B 的 pure style pattern：verbose OR ~10.5 \n      (略低于 Qwen 13.10，因为 GPT-4o style sensitivity 系统性弱于 Qwen)，\n      originality OR ~0.55 NS（方向一致——concise text 不因 content 被偏好，bias 完全来自 verbose style）。\n      Cross-judge GEE gradient 一致：verbosity pure style > formality mixed > register originality-dominated。\n      \n      (5) API cost ~$19 可控（200 verbosity pairwise + 200 Likert + 188 register pairwise + 188 register Likert\n      ≈ 776 API calls × ~$0.025/call）。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Complete 2×3 Evidence Matrix (median tier final)\"\n        content: |\n          |            | GPT-4o BT [CI]              | GPT-4o Likert p | Qwen3-32B BT [CI]           | Qwen3-32B Likert p | Blindspot |\n          |-----------|---------------------------|-----------------|---------------------------|-------------------|-----------|\n          | Formality  | 63.0% [55.8, 70.3]***      | 0.332           | 66.5% [58.5, 73.9]****     | 0.908             | 2/2 ✅    |\n          | Verbosity  | 78.0% [70.0, 85.0]****     | 0.22            | 77.3% [70.3, 84.3]****     | 0.179             | 2/2 ✅    |\n          | Register   | 58.0% [50.0, 66.0] (NS)    | 0.55            | GEE OR=1.91 [1.01, 3.58]*  | 0.505             | 1/2 ✅    |\n      - name: \"Cross-judge GEE gradient (complete)\"\n        content: |\n          | Axis       | Judge     | Style OR | Style p  | Origin. OR | Origin. p | Classification       |\n          |-----------|----------|---------|----------|-----------|----------|---------------------|\n          | Verbosity  | Qwen3-32B | 13.10   | <10⁻⁹   | 0.49 (NS) | 0.096    | Pure style           |\n          | Verbosity  | GPT-4o    | 10.50   | <10⁻⁷   | 0.55 (NS) | 0.15     | Pure style           |\n          | Formality  | Qwen3-32B | 4.20    | 0.0002   | 4.70      | <0.0001  | Mixed                |\n          | Formality  | GPT-4o    | 2.21    | 0.010    | 1.82      | 0.052    | Mixed (marginal)     |\n          | Register   | Qwen3-32B | 1.91    | 0.046    | 5.72      | <0.0001  | Originality-dominated |\n          | Register   | GPT-4o    | 1.75    | 0.08     | 3.50      | 0.002    | Originality-dominated |\n    figures_description:\n      - >\n        Forest plot (Figure 3, final): 6 rows (2 judges × 3 axes), x-axis = BT win probability,\n        dashed line at 0.50. Verbosity cells 最右 (0.77–0.78), formality 中间 (0.62–0.665),\n        register 接近 0.50 (0.58). 视觉上清晰分离三档。\n      - >\n        GEE gradient scatter: x = style OR (log scale), y = originality OR (log scale),\n        6 points 按 axis 着色 (verbosity 蓝, formality 绿, register 红), 按 judge 标记 (圆/方)。\n        Verbosity 右下角 (high style, low originality), register 左上角 (low style, high originality),\n        formality 对角线上 (both moderate)。两个 judge 的同轴点紧密聚类 → cross-judge consistency。\n    analysis: >\n      exp-020 完成后，median 档的证据结构完整：\n      - C1: CSD pipeline detects style bias across 2 judges × 3 axes (5/6 primary cells significant)\n      - C2: Likert Blindspot confirmed in 5/6 cells; mechanism = tie-induced power deficit\n      - C3: GEE gradient consistent across judges — verbosity pure → formality mixed → register originality-dominated\n      - C4: Practitioner guidance grounded in complete 2×3 matrix\n      \n      Forest plot + GEE gradient visualization 构成两个 key figures，配合 power curve (Figure 1) \n      和 pipeline diagram (Figure 2) = 4 figures total（比 planned 3 多 1，但 GEE scatter \n      可以 inline 在 results section 不占 figure slot）。\n      \n      Expected review score 3.0–3.5 的支撑：\n      - Evidence depth: 2×3 matrix complete, BT + GEE + ordinal regression, NLI validation\n      - Writing quality: 3 figures (power curve + pipeline + forest plot), ≤8.5 pages, 22+ refs\n      - Novelty cap: Likert Blindspot is domain transfer of known psychometric phenomenon → Findings\n      - Risk: new reviewer scores novelty ≤2.5 → need writing + evidence to compensate to 3.0 floor\n```","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"fe4f732d-0abd-4b87-8c2d-8b5d94071a71","total_cost_usd":0.70173475,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":22645,"cache_read_input_tokens":11841,"output_tokens":21463,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":22645,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":21463,"cache_read_input_tokens":11841,"cache_creation_input_tokens":22645,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":22645},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":17603,"outputTokens":19,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":0,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.017698000000000002,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000},"claude-opus-4-6":{"inputTokens":2,"outputTokens":21463,"cacheReadInputTokens":11841,"cacheCreationInputTokens":22645,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.68403675,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":64000}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","uuid":"6697dab3-f728-42e9-b153-921364e533c5"}
